        -:  689: * about what happens (raw / lossy / clamped) and stdout's sanitizer renders
        -:  690: * every one of them identically, so the defect is invisible in printed
        -:  691: * output -- only the bytes show it.
        -:  692: *
        -:  693: * Every C slice implementation reports the range it is about to return here.
        -:  694: * NOTHING FAILS: this records and (level-gated) logs. The hard error is
        -:  695: * stage 4 and is enabled only once the measured blast radius over a real
        -:  696: * workload is zero or a justified residual.
        -:  697: *
        -:  698: * Gate -- DEFAULT OFF -- environment `SIMPLE_UTF8_SLICE_AUDIT`:
        -:  699: *   unset / "0"  disabled; one relaxed load per slice, no validation
        -:  700: *   "1"          count violations, log the FIRST occurrence per site
        -:  701: *   "2"          count violations, log EVERY occurrence
        -:  702: *
        -:  703: * A violation is recorded only when the SOURCE bytes were valid UTF-8 and
        -:  704: * the returned bytes are not, so the count measures what slicing causes
        -:  705: * rather than inheriting unrelated corruption.
        -:  706: * ================================================================ */
